---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import SiteHeader from "../components/SiteHeader.astro";
import SiteFooter from "../components/SiteFooter.astro";
import "../styles/content.css";

const commands = [
  ["raohane launcher", "Open Launcher 2.0 with apps, native actions and search modes."],
  ["raohane control", "Open the native Control Center."],
  ["raohane settings", "Open the Raohane Settings workspace."],
  ["raohane media", "Open the media surface owned by the current scene and placement policy."],
  ["raohane desktop", "Open desktop actions and wallpaper tools."],
  ["raohane wallpaper", "Open the wallpaper selector directly."],
  ["raohane session", "Open session actions such as lock, logout and power controls."],
  ["raohane translate", "Start the screen-translation workflow."],
];
---

<BaseLayout title="Docs — Raohane" description="Raohane commands, configuration paths, Launcher 2.0 search grammar, diagnostics and development reference.">
  <div class="page-shell">
    <SiteHeader active="docs" />
    <main id="main-content" class="content-main shell-width">
      <section class="page-intro">
        <span class="page-badge">Reference · Raohane 1.2.1</span>
        <h1>Know the shell.<br/><em>Keep control.</em></h1>
        <p>A compact operational reference for daily use, configuration and recovery. The deeper architecture, release validation and developer notes stay next to the runtime source.</p>
      </section>

      <section class="docs-overview" aria-label="Documentation scope">
        <div><b>CLI</b><span>Direct shell entry points</span></div>
        <div><b>State</b><span>Config, runtime and scene data</span></div>
        <div><b>Recovery</b><span>Doctor, logs and validation</span></div>
      </section>

      <div class="docs-layout">
        <aside class="docs-nav" aria-label="Documentation sections">
          <a href="#commands">Commands</a>
          <a href="#launcher">Launcher</a>
          <a href="#configuration">Configuration</a>
          <a href="#scenes">Scenes</a>
          <a href="#themes">Themes</a>
          <a href="#diagnostics">Diagnostics</a>
          <a href="#development">Development</a>
        </aside>

        <article class="docs-article">
          <section id="commands">
            <span class="section-kicker">01 · Daily use</span>
            <h2>Primary commands</h2>
            <p>The <code>raohane</code> CLI is a thin entry layer over native Raohane services and surfaces. Use it for direct access, scripting and recovery without replacing the shell's internal service ownership.</p>
            <div class="command-ledger">
              {commands.map(([command, description]) => (
                <div><code>{command}</code><span>{description}</span></div>
              ))}
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="launcher">
            <span class="section-kicker">02 · Search grammar</span>
            <h2>Launcher 2.0</h2>
            <p>Launcher combines applications with context-aware Raohane actions. Prefixes switch the search model without opening another utility.</p>
            <div class="command-ledger">
              <div><code>/</code><span>Raohane actions and shell commands exposed by the action registry.</span></div>
              <div><code>&gt;</code><span>Command execution mode.</span></div>
              <div><code>=</code><span>Calculator mode.</span></div>
              <div><code>:</code><span>Clipboard history mode.</span></div>
            </div>
          </section>

          <section id="configuration">
            <span class="section-kicker">03 · User state</span>
            <h2>Configuration</h2>
            <p>Primary product settings live in <code>~/.config/raohane/native.json</code>. User autostart commands belong in <code>~/.config/raohane/autostart.conf</code>. Runtime-only scene state is kept separate so automatic context switching does not rewrite the user's base configuration.</p>
            <div class="docs-callout">Prefer changing product settings through Raohane Settings. Direct JSON edits are useful for recovery or development, but malformed values may be normalized during schema upgrades.</div>
          </section>

          <section id="scenes">
            <span class="section-kicker">04 · Context</span>
            <h2>Scenes</h2>
            <p>Balanced, Gaming, Focus and Work are runtime policy layers. Application-aware switching can temporarily change DND, Keep Awake, Game Mode and other scene-owned behavior, then return to the user's selected scene without permanently overwriting settings.</p>
            <div class="docs-callout">Gaming is intentionally reversible. Closing the matching game or leaving the rule context restores the selected scene and its baseline policies.</div>
          </section>

          <section id="themes">
            <span class="section-kicker">05 · Appearance</span>
            <h2>Themes</h2>
            <p>Raohane uses one whole-shell token system across Settings, Launcher, Control Center, media, widgets and desktop surfaces. Built-in presets can be extended with user themes.</p>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>raohane theme list
raohane theme import FILE
raohane theme export ID FILE
raohane theme remove ID</code></pre></div>
          </section>

          <section id="diagnostics">
            <span class="section-kicker">06 · Recovery</span>
            <h2>Diagnostics</h2>
            <p>Start with the complete doctor report. It checks dependencies, installed runtime integrity, services, graphics and shell context before you start changing configuration blindly.</p>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>raohane doctor all
raohane status
raohane logs</code></pre></div>
            <h3>Inspect startup errors directly</h3>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>raohane stop
raohane run</code></pre></div>
            <p>For a performance report, include the installed version, recent logs, process usage during the issue and the exact interaction that triggered it.</p>
          </section>

          <section id="development">
            <span class="section-kicker">07 · Source</span>
            <h2>Development</h2>
            <p>Product QML lives under <code>modules/raohane/</code>. Static audits validate source/runtime boundaries, localization and architectural contracts, but final release validation still needs a real Hyprland + Quickshell session.</p>
            <div class="code-panel"><pre><code>bash scripts/raohane-audit.sh
bash scripts/runtime-payload-audit.sh
bash scripts/media-overlay-boundary-audit.sh</code></pre></div>
            <p><a class="button button-ghost" href="https://github.com/killmyselfrin/raohane-dots/tree/main/docs" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Open source documentation ↗</a></p>
          </section>
        </article>
      </div>
    </main>
    <SiteFooter />
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
